course: dictionary
lesson: 8358
title: Rotation: turning and taking turns
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Rotation means turning around a centre point or a line. The Earth's rotation is its spin on its own axis, and that spin makes day and night.
explain: Rotation can also mean taking turns in a fixed order. «Changing the crop in each field from year to year is called crop rotation.» Here, rotation means the farmer changes the crops in the same place, one after another, so the land stays healthy.
explain: Check the clues around the word. If the sentence talks about turning, spinning or angles, rotation means a turn. If it talks about taking turns or doing jobs in order, rotation means taking turns.
fact: A rotation is one complete turn around a centre point.
fact: A quarter rotation is a turn of 90 degrees.
fact: The Earth's rotation takes about 24 hours and makes day and night.
fact: Crop rotation means growing different crops in a field each year to keep the soil healthy.
fact: Things done in rotation are done in a fixed order, so each person gets a fair turn.
exercise: In maths, how many degrees is a quarter rotation? | *90 degrees | 360 degrees | 180 degrees | 45 degrees
exercise: «Changing the crop in each field from year to year is called crop rotation.» What is the name for this? | Soil digging | *Crop rotation | Field sweeping | Harvest day
exercise: Roughly how long does the Earth take to make one rotation on its axis? | About 365 days | About 1 hour | About 12 hours | *About 24 hours
test: If the children do the jobs in rotation, what happens? | Nobody has to help | *Each child takes a turn in a fixed order | Jobs are done at random | Only one child does all the jobs
test: Which words describe a rotation in maths? | A shape gets bigger | *A shape turns around a fixed point | A shape is cut in half | A shape is coloured in
exam: Which phrase means a shape looks the same after part of a turn? | Clockwise sum | Quarter bend | Crop rotation | *Rotational symmetry
